E-313- PO FITAP WHO MUST BE INCLUDED IN THE ASSISTANCE UNIT

The assistance must include:

● The minor unmarried parent's child(ren);

● The minor unmarried parent;

● The minor unmarried parent's siblings under age 18, including half siblings and legal step siblings;

● The minor unmarried parent's parents;

● The parents of the dependent children who are included; and

● The minor unmarried parent's legal stepparent.

See C-121-FITAP for exceptions to inclusion in the certification.

Note: Eligibility must be determined for two-parent households. Two-parent households are not eligible for FITAP cash assistance unless at least one parent is determined to be physically or mentally incapacitated or caring for a disabled family member living in the home. (See * C-1510- FITAP **).

E-314- PO FITAP CHILD SUPPORT

If either or both of the parents of the minor unmarried parent are absent from the home, referral must be made on the absent parents of the minor unmarried parent as well as on the absent parent of the child.

Both the minor unmarried parent and the payee are required to cooperate with Child Support Enforcement (CSE).

